From: shahed <jamshidalinezhadian@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:54:17 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] camera2: port the legacy shim to the Android 15 QPR2
 camera2 API

LineageOS 22.2 (android-15.0.0_r32) changed two interfaces the HALv1
legacy shim sits on:

- ICameraDeviceCallbacks.onResultReceived() takes a CameraMetadataInfo
  union (metadata, or the size of an entry in a result FMQ) instead of
  CameraMetadataNative, and onClientSharedAccessPriorityChanged() was
  added. LegacyCameraDevice wraps its metadata with
  CameraMetadataInfo.metadata(), and the shim's callback thread passes
  the union through; camera sharing is not offered on this path.
- ICameraDeviceUser gained getCaptureResultMetadataQueue() and
  isPrimaryClient(). The shim has no result FMQ, since it delivers the
  metadata in each callback, so it returns null, and CameraDeviceImpl
  only creates its FMQ reader when a queue exists. The shim's device is
  never shared, so it is always the primary client.
